ent API for fetching URLs and extracting and manipulating data, using the best of HTML5 DOM methods and CSS selectors. jsoup implements the WHATWG HTML5 specification, and parses HTML to the same DOM as modern browsers do."},"location": {"uri": "file://\/home\/runner\/.m2\/repository\/org\/jsoup\/jsoup\/1.15.3\/jsoup-1.15.3.jar"},"hashes": {"md5": "4f16c3b17b8c1b0173b1ed9f99f2c27c","sha1": "f6e1d8a8819f854b681c8eaa57fd59a42329e10c","sha256": "e20a5e78b1372f2a4e620832db4442d5077e5cbde280b24c666a3770844999bc"},"properties": {"license": "The MIT License: https:\/\/jsoup.org\/license","id18": "pkg:maven\/org.jsoup\/jsoup@1.15.3","vid7": "cpe:2.3:a:jsoup:jsoup:1.15.3:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"}},{"description": {"text": "JSR305 Annotations for Findbugs"},"location": {"uri": "file://\/home\/runner\/.m2\/repository\/com\/google\/code\/findbugs\/jsr305\/3.0.2\/jsr305-3.0.2.jar"},"hashes": {"md5": "dd83accb899363c32b07d7a1b2e4ce40","sha1": "25ea2e8b0c338a877313bd4672d3fe056ea78f0d","sha256": "766ad2a0783f2687962c8ad74ceecc38a28b9f72a2d085ee438b7813e928d0c7"},"properties": {"license": "The Apache Software License, Version 2.0: http:\/\/www.apache.org\/licenses\/LICENSE-2.0.txt","id19": "pkg:maven\/com.google.code.findbugs\/jsr305@3.0.2"}},{"description": {"text": "A lightweight library of useful, mostly pure functions"},"location": {"uri": "file://\/home\/runner\/.m2\/repository\/dev\/weavejester\/medley\/1.8.1\/medley-1.8.1.jar"},"hashes": {"md5": "2aa0e85a14ea0275b857b8f6aa085722","sha1": "9940f1e5411a2760d54ff21566257bc0427fafe5","sha256": "0a8492f5c46d110f8e2003056733b6b62911e2bd204ea8119b8edacd33adc2d5"},"properties": {"license": "Eclipse Public License: http:\/\/www.eclipse.org\/legal\/epl-v10.html","id20": "pkg:maven\/dev.weavejester\/medley@1.8.1"}},{"description": {"text": "A micro-library for Clojure that provides first class support for named-capturing groups in regular expressions."},"location": {"uri": "file://\/home\/runner\/.m2\/repository\/com\/github\/pmonks\/rencg\/1.0.51\/rencg-1.0.51.jar"},"hashes": {"md5": "57d5cb137b1955a15fadc6074da8550d","sha1": "bdd0836b60caf5ee0bdadeb4de20dd87c1398ab3","sha256": "82f0ff7e7e1aa63d27b593faaa6f0a9d15af32623bbcea1d825368315110d70d"},"properties": {"license": "Apache-2.0: http:\/\/www.apache.org\/licenses\/LICENSE-2.0.html","id21": "pkg:maven\/com.github.pmonks\/rencg@1.0.51"}},{"description": {"text": "The slf4j API"},"location": {"uri": "file://\/home\/runner\/.m2\/repository\/org\/slf4j\/slf4j-api\/2.0.13\/slf4j-api-2.0.13.jar"},"hashes": {"md5": "7f4028aa04f75427327f3f30cd62ba4e","sha1": "80229737f704b121a318bba5d5deacbcf395bc77","sha256": "e7c2a48e8515ba1f49fa637d57b4e2f590b3f5bd97407ac699c3aa5efb1204a9"},"properties": {"license": "http:\/\/www.opensource.org\/licenses\/mit-license.php","id22": "pkg:maven\/org.slf4j\/slf4j-api@2.0.13"}},{"description": {"text": "Specification of data and functions"},"location": {"uri": "file://\/home\/runner\/.m2\/repository\/org\/clojure\/spec.alpha\/0.5.238\/spec.alpha-0.5.238.jar"},"hashes": {"md5": "9f5ea5239dc04d6a8115add1e4f5f23a","sha1": "4eb5dea521c4e6e1f68c2c47517f14a922003e60","sha256": "94cd99b6ea639641f37af4860a643b6ed399ee5a8be5d717cff0b663c8d75077"},"properties": {"license": "Eclipse Public License 1.0: https:\/\/opensource.org\/license\/epl-1-0\/","id23": "pkg:maven\/org.clojure\/spec.alpha@0.5.238"}},{"location": {"uri": "file://\/home\/runner\/.m2\/repository\/org\/clojure\/tools.logging\/1.3.0\/tools.logging-1.3.0.jar"},"hashes": {"md5": "b6b3c2ffeb27a25eab2d6e0e3a6e6b57","sha1": "07d45477c1b61230b0d1fcf36afccc02155a4b32","sha256": "826969b78d9ada327de6b7da0f176457d95614fa38c280326610f31a6b515c91"},"properties": {"id24": "pkg:maven\/org.clojure\/tools.logging@1.3.0","vid8": "cpe:2.3:a:alex_project:alex:1.3.0:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"}},{"description": {"text": "your friendly XML navigator"},"location": {"uri": "file://\/home\/runner\/.m2\/repository\/tolitius\/xml-in\/0.1.1\/xml-in-0.1.1.jar"},"hashes": {"md5": "754502ef9d8c1574d6d893b22f6101dc","sha1": "0a68865842a0fa7484bca3a7be33f182d8213a97","sha256": "43ab632812fe03b86b1a154723d809bb393e11a0ff0e6677167f14ece40f5543"},"properties": {"license": "Eclipse Public License: http:\/\/www.eclipse.org\/legal\/epl-v10.html","id25": "pkg:maven\/tolitius\/xml-in@0.1.1"}}],"results": [ {"ruleId": "CVE-2025-48734","level": "warning","message": {"text": "CVE-2025-48734 - Improper Access Control vulnerability in Apache Commons.\n\n\n\nA special BeanIntrospector class was added in version 1.9.2. This can be used to stop attackers from using the declared class property of Java enum objects to get access to the classloader. However this protection was not enabled by default. PropertyUtilsBean (and consequently BeanUtilsBean) now disallows declared class level property access by default.\n\n\n\n\n\nReleases 1.11.0 and 2.0.0-M2 address a potential security issue when accessing enum properties in an uncontrolled way. If an application using Commons BeanUtils passes property paths from an external source directly to the getProperty() method of PropertyUtilsBean, an attacker can access the enum\u2019s class loader via the \u201CdeclaredClass\u201D property available on all Java \u201Cenum\u201D objects. Accessing the enum\u2019s \u201CdeclaredClass\u201D allows remote attackers to access the ClassLoader and execute arbitrary code. The same issue exists with PropertyUtilsBean.getNestedProperty().\nStarting in versions 1.11.0 and 2.0.0-M2 a special BeanIntrospector suppresses the \u201CdeclaredClass\u201D property. Note that this new BeanIntrospector is enabled by default, but you can disable it to regain the old behavior; see section 2.5 of the user's guide and the unit tests.\n\nThis issue affects Apache Commons BeanUtils 1.x before 1.11.0, and 2.x before 2.0.0-M2.Users of the artifact commons-beanutils:commons-beanutils\n\n 1.x are recommended to upgrade to version 1.11.0, which fixes the issue.\n\n\nUsers of the artifact org.apache.commons:commons-beanutils2\n\n 2.x are recommended to upgrade to version 2.0.0-M2, which fixes the issue."},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "eb5f8cf1401189092840e52c25d48e77"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/home\/runner\/.m2\/repository\/commons-beanutils\/commons-beanutils\/1.9.4\/commons-beanutils-1.9.4.jar","index": 4 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:maven\/commons-beanutils\/commons-beanutils@1.9.4"}]}]}, {"ruleId": "CVE-2025-48924","level": "warning","message": {"text": "CVE-2025-48924 - Uncontrolled Recursion vulnerability in Apache Commons Lang.\n\nThis issue affects Apache Commons Lang: Starting with\u00A0commons-lang:commons-lang\u00A02.0 to 2.6, and, from org.apache.commons:commons-lang3 3.0 before\u00A03.18.0.\n\nThe methods ClassUtils.getClass(...) can throw\u00A0StackOverflowError on very long inputs. Because an Error is usually not handled by applications and libraries, a \nStackOverflowError could\u00A0cause an application to stop.\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 3.18.0, which fixes the issue."},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "065ac7df188e8c80a7c2979bc5e08183"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/home\/runner\/.m2\/repository\/org\/apache\/commons\/commons-lang3\/3.5\/commons-lang3-3.5.jar","index": 7 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:maven\/org.apache.commons\/commons-lang3@3.5"}]}]}, {"ruleId": "CVE-2025-53864","level": "warning","message": {"text": "CVE-2025-53864 - github.com\/sigstore\/sigstore-java (gson) - Stack-based Buffer Overflow [CVE-2025-53864]\n\nA stack-based buffer overflow condition is a condition where the buffer being overwritten is allocated on the stack (i.e., is a local variable or, rarely, a parameter to a function)."},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "bdde1d2053ecd443a21ad292134618d4"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/home\/runner\/.m2\/repository\/com\/google\/code\/gson\/gson\/2.8.9\/gson-2.8.9.jar","index": 13 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:maven\/com.google.code.gson\/gson@2.8.9"}]}]}]}]}